        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Harar</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1216 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The date is unclear; the semi-legendary Fath Madinat Harar names the saint Abadir Umar ar-Rida as founder about 612 AH (1216 CE), while other accounts give Qurayshi settlers in the late 7th century or a local creation in the 10th century.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On a hilltop on the Harar plateau in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, at an elevation of 1,885 metres and about 500 kilometres from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The walled old city with its five gates; the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> from 1520; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Ghazi</a>'s base against Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Harar with its own coinage; its mosques and shrines; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> trade; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a>'s conquest in 1887; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harari">Harari</a> houses</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Harar is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harari">Harari</a> Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, and its old walled city, Harar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugol">Jugol</a>, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</span></div>
