    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Harar was a Muslim trading town on the Harar plateau, founded according to tradition by the saint Abadir Umar ar-Rida about 1216, and in 1520 it became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a>.</li><li>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> it was ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wazir">wazirs</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">Imamate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aussa">Aussa</a> and then, from the 17th century, by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> of the Dawud dynasty, who minted their own coins and made it a religious centre.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> held it from the 1870s to 1885, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> conquered it in 1887, Italian forces held it from 1936 to 1941, and it later became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harari">Harari</a> Region.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The red earth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harari">Harari</a> house floors is supposed to recall the blood shed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chelenqo">Battle of Chelenqo</a> in 1887, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> Abdullahi and took the city.</p></aside>
    </section>

